<title>USA: SAN ANTONIO FEEDER CATTLE STEADY-UP $2 - USDA.</title>
<headline>SAN ANTONIO FEEDER CATTLE STEADY-UP $2 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>SAN ANTONIO 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Compared to Monday - Feeder steers steady, except over 700 lbs $2.00 per cwt higher. Feeder heifers mostly steady, USDA said.</p>
<p>Bulk of supply Medium and Large 1-2 300-600 lb feeder steers and heifers. Supply included 8 percent cows and bulls, 41 percent feeder cattle over 600 lbs. Receipts - 448  Last Week - 338  Last Year - 1,190</p>
<p>Feeder Steers - Medium and Large 1 - 600-700 lbs 72.25-79.75, pkg 81.50; 700-800 lbs 70.50-77.00; pkg 805 lbs 76.50. Medium and Large 1-2 - pkg 240 lbs 82.00; 300-400 lbs 75.50-84.50, two pkgs 88.25-90.00; 400-500 lbs 75.50-83.00; 500-600 lbs 74.50-76.50; few 600-700 lbs 68.50-72.50; few 800-925 lbs 63.50-65.50.</p>
<p>Feeder Heifers - Medium and Large 1 - 600-650 lbs 73.00-77.50; pkg 770 lbs 70.25. Medium and Large 1-2 - 300-575 lbs 70.00-75.25; pkg 675 lbs 61.00; pkg 860 lbs 63.50.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
